findings=[
('P0','01','Name the build before approving a redesign','BASELINE_UPDATE.md; .git/refs/heads/main; CodeGraph status','The supplied e9b5acb baseline was superseded during this audit. The branch reference now reads deeea2e; graph counts also changed.','Pin the operator review to deeea2e and retain a visible provenance strip. Reopen approval if another source is located.','Prevents polishing an obsolete interface and attributing old defects to new work.','Reconciliation delays implementation; it avoids duplicated work.','Operator confirms served build and intended source.','Reviewer can identify the revision and capture viewport without opening developer tools.','Accept deeea2e as the review baseline; do not treat tree equivalence as newly verified.','setup'),
('P0','02','Give the first rally one clear route','index.html #title-modal, #btn-start-match; DOCS/ARCHITECTURE.md §1','Setup combines four steps, explanatory text, a miniature court, three strong start actions and the live HUD.','Retain four numbered summaries and ready defaults. Make Play Now the only solid action; keep Wonder Demo and Watch AI as visible secondary choices.','A stable action hierarchy reduces scanning while preserving the wonder-first invitation.','Less initial exposition; the full setup remains editable.','Initialization readiness and existing start/intro/spectator handlers.','From ready page load, 4 of 5 first-time participants begin a rally within 30 seconds without coaching; measure load time separately.','Approve Play Now as primary, Wonder Demo as the featured secondary route.','setup'),
('P0','03','Reflow the HUD instead of compressing it','styles.css:2–3; #top-hud-bar; before-game-portrait.png','Portrait retains broad left/right toolbar groups; controls crowd the score and extend beyond the visible width.','Use score + match status + Menu in a compact header. Keep six shot actions in a 3×2 grid and move camera/audio/help into a named menu.','Protects court visibility and gives thumbs predictable targets.','Some secondary actions take one extra tap.','Responsive layout and safe-area handling.','At 390×844 and 844×390 every primary action is reachable, with no horizontal page scroll or overlap; targets at least 44×44 CSS px.','Approve separate portrait and landscape compositions.','game'),
('P0','04','Connection must mean acknowledged connection','public/companion.html #conn-badge, sendSwing, telemetry interval','The phone page says Connected on arrival. Source hardcodes that label; requests swallow network errors and do not check response.ok.','Distinguish Not paired, Connecting, Connected, Reconnecting and Server unavailable. Show room/player identity and last acknowledged input.','Truthful feedback prevents repeated swings and false confidence.','Requires a small status contract, not just copy changes.','Backend acknowledgment, heartbeat timeout and room identity.','With backend offline, never show Connected; recover after reconnect without sending stale strokes or changing player assignment.','Approve acknowledgment-based connection status before promoting phone play.','companion'),
('P0','05','Make permission recovery a first-class route','public/companion.html permission handler; README Controls and modes','Permission results are not checked before the Active label; bindSensors runs on load and again after enable. No camera or mic was granted in this audit.','Separate connection from sensor permission. Explain the request, offer touch-only play, show denied/unsupported states and a retry path.','People understand what is missing and retain a usable alternative.','Additional state design and physical-device testing.','Browser permission outcomes, HTTPS deployment and sensor capability detection.','Denied, unavailable and allowed outcomes each have truthful labels; listeners bind once; touch actions remain usable without motion permission.','Approve touch fallback and explicit Experimental phone labeling.','companion'),
('P1','06','Make setup work without hover','index.html setup-step-1 through setup-step-4; styles.css:145–151','The interface explicitly instructs users to hover or select to reveal steps; panels use max-height and overflow hiding.','Use explicit disclosure buttons with expanded state, retained summaries and visible selection marks. Preserve opponent, spectator/1v1, court, scoring, footwork/referee/camera.','Touch, keyboard and remote users receive the same sequence.','Expanded setup can require vertical scrolling.','Accessible disclosure semantics and existing preference state.','Tab/Enter can open all four steps; selected values survive collapse; 200% zoom exposes all choices.','Approve click/keyboard disclosure with no hover dependency.','setup'),
('P1','07','Use type size to express importance','styles.css:3, 162–176; before-setup-desktop.png','Several setup helpers and toolbar labels are around 10–12px, bold and uppercase; many compete with the score.','Use the supplied Inter stack, 16px body, 14px metadata, 24–32px section titles and tabular score numerals. Reserve heavy weight for score and primary actions.','Readable rhythm makes the product feel deliberate without losing its arcade personality.','Slightly fewer controls fit on the first view.','Responsive layout and actual font availability.','No essential instruction below 14px on desktop or 16px in phone controls; TV labels tested at viewing distance.','Approve typography hierarchy, retaining supplied brand fonts.','setup'),
('P1','08','Replace color competition with explicit state','styles.css:1–3, shot-chip, wii-green-choice, let-call-chip','Cyan, green, yellow, gold, purple and red borders/gradients all signal importance. Selection depends heavily on color.','Use white/surface neutrals, one blue accent and text/check marks for selection. Reserve contextual state words for errors, connection and experimental modes.','A consistent visual grammar reduces search cost and works without color perception.','Less decorative shine; court and character animation retain energy.','Token mapping and contrast verification.','Text contrast ≥4.5:1, large text/icons ≥3:1 across default/hover/focus; selected states identifiable in grayscale.','Approve quieter chrome while preserving the real game artwork.','game'),
('P1','09','Keep the shot vocabulary and make timing readable','index.html .squash-shot-selector-row, #timing-gauge-card; before-game-desktop.png','Drive, Cut Drop, Boast, Lob, Kill and Let are available; timing labels are tiny and far from the score.','Retain all six actions, show selected shot text and a wider three-region timing meter. Teach hold/release and Shift cut alongside the first serve.','Preserves depth while reducing memory burden for beginners.','A larger input dock occupies some court-adjacent space.','Shot handler mappings, preparation state and pointer cancellation.','Keys 1–5 and F/L remain valid; hold/release, cancel and focus loss cannot produce unintended shots; labels remain legible on phones.','Approve the six-action dock and explicit timing labels.','game'),
('P1','10','Separate help from live play and tuning','index.html #controls-guide-modal, #squash-rules-modal; before-controls-desktop.png','Controls successfully opens Rules and Rules resumes play; the accessibility tree still exposes background HUD controls. Focus remains on the opening control in observed snapshots.','Use one modal owner, move focus into the dialog, make background inert, pause safely and restore focus on close. Tune Lab becomes a distinct workspace.','Prevents accidental shots while reading and establishes predictable keyboard behavior.','Requires shared overlay state rather than separate booleans.','Pause/resume policy and input routing.','Tab stays inside help; Escape closes only the top surface; game hotkeys do not fire while typing or reading; focus returns to opener.','Approve a single overlay policy; verify existing pause semantics before wiring.','controls'),
('P1','11','Teach rules in layers, keep the reference','index.html #squash-rules-modal; before-rules-desktop.png','Rules presents a long official-reference panel with dense court, scoring, serve and interference sections.','Lead with a concise game guide and a persistent Call Let explanation; place complete rules and external authority links under named sections. Preserve PAR 11, Arcade 5 and Hi-Ho 9.','Novices can act immediately while experts retain reference depth.','Editorial review is needed to avoid changing rules meaning.','RulesEngine/source alignment; current governing-body review before release.','A user can locate serve, scoring and interference within 10 seconds; no claim of certification; no blocked access to full reference.','Approve layered help, with rules accuracy reviewed separately.','rules'),
('P1','12','Let Wonder Demo own the stage','before-wonder-desktop.png; DOCS/ARCHITECTURE.md §1 and IntroDirector','Wonder starts correctly, but narrator promotion and demo commentary can coexist with center banners and the full HUD.','Use one caption channel, progress A/B, explicit Skip/Replay and a clear handoff to Play. Preserve spectacular kill and gentle drop.','Attention stays on geometry, disguise and the nick rather than competing messages.','Requires arbitration between narrator, referee and intro messages.','IntroDirector and audio narration scheduling.','During either demo only one teaching caption is visible; skip exits reliably; reduced-motion setting removes flashes/zoom while preserving explanation.','Approve a focused two-part demonstration, not a mandatory tutorial.','wonder'),
('P1','13','Give Tune Lab a safe experimental workspace','src/squash/TuningPanel.js:120–160, 167–263; before-tuning-desktop.png','A narrow live drawer contains presets, small controls, sliders, nick scenarios and diagnostics over active court play.','Separate Presets, Physics, Shot & Cut, Move & AI, Nick Lab, A/B and Diagnostics. Show units, changed values, reset scope and Live/Paused status.','Experts can manipulate a hypothesis without hiding the consequences or confusing tuning with ordinary settings.','Larger workspace; beginner path stays simpler.','TuningStore undo/snapshot behavior and pause policy.','Every slider has a programmatic label and exact numeric input; reset states its scope; import reports validation before apply.','Approve expert workspace and preservation of all current tuning operations.','tuning'),
('P1','14','Keep evidence attached to A/B results','src/squash/TuningPanel.js:397–425; before-nicklab-desktop.png; before-diagnostics-desktop.png','A/B compares identical scenarios; Diagnostics displayed 15/15 passed. That display does not prove phone, camera or physical squash correctness.','Attach preset names, seed, configuration hash, units and run time to every comparison. Separate simulator checks from runtime/device acceptance.','Makes results repeatable and prevents an automated pass being mistaken for product readiness.','More metadata and export requirements.','Deterministic runner and export schema.','Same seed/config reproduces trajectory within documented tolerance; exported report contains provenance; UI never labels untested devices verified.','Approve separate simulation and physical-device evidence gates.','tuning'),
('P1','15','Distinguish court camera from input camera','index.html #btn-top-camera-cycle, #btn-webcam-toggle, #btn-camera-facing; src/motion_controls.js','Court view cycling appears twice; Pose Cam and handedness sit elsewhere. Updated source includes camera placement/interpretation paths.','Use Court view for Back Glass/Front Wall/High Gallery/Corner Nick/Overhead T; Input camera for front/rear, placement and mirrored preview. Keep handedness explicit.','Eliminates ambiguity between watching the court and capturing the player.','One extra group in settings.','Camera mode handler and biomechanical coordinate conventions.','Court-view changes do not request permission; input-camera changes explain permission; right/left and mirrored/rear combinations validated on hardware.','Approve separate names and no automatic camera activation.','camera'),
('P2','16','Preserve the soundtrack with calmer audio controls','before-audio-desktop.png; src/audio_engine.js; index.html #jukebox-modal','Updated Jukebox exposes 14 tracks, auto/locked/shuffle modes and referee controls; the HUD repeats audio actions.','Keep one Sound entry with current track and mute state. In Jukebox separate music, court effects and referee/narrator; label Next/Previous rather than relying on glyphs.','The soundtrack remains a product feature while speech and game feedback become easier to manage.','Independent volume controls may require audio routing work.','Existing audio engine and browser autoplay rules.','Mute state is explicit; keyboard names announce Next track; referee calls remain available when music is muted if independent mixing is approved.','Approve grouping; decide whether independent narrator/referee volume is in scope.','audio'),
('P1','17','Design for the couch and for reduced motion','styles.css animations and media query; README TV boundary','The source uses pulsing indicators and animated banners; no prefers-reduced-motion rule was found. Dedicated Cast support is not established.','Offer reduced motion, a readable TV presentation mode and keyboard/remote focus order. Keep screen mirroring described separately from Cast support.','Respects motion sensitivity and distance viewing without inventing platform capabilities.','Requires real TV/WebView and remote testing.','Animation controls, input mapping and display-safe margins.','Reduced-motion disables nonessential pulses/zoom; all actions operable by keyboard; test at 1920×1080 from 2–3 metres; do not claim Cast certification.','Approve TV readability target, defer unsupported receiver promises.','game'),
('P1','18','Show readiness before inviting interaction','BASELINE_UPDATE.md; final working captures; live-actions.json','Early startup observations came from an unprovisioned checkout. The updated parent note reports 13 local assets downloaded; after reload, game and panels worked. This is a resilience opportunity, not a persistent current-build defect.','Show Preparing court with a meaningful status; enable start when handlers/assets are ready, with retry and keyboard fallback on failure.','Prevents an initial silent response from being interpreted as a broken game.','A readiness gate must not hide partial-load recovery.','Asset/module lifecycle and timeout reporting.','Under throttled network, no apparently ready inactive start button; failure explains recovery; warm/cold first-rally times reported separately.','Approve readiness state; early behavior is not a persistent gameplay failure.','setup')]

